			"notes": "## New features\n\n**Trophy Frog HUD (Fishing → Trophy Frogs)**\n- Shows your Trophy Frog catches per frog and tier (Bronze / Silver / Gold / Diamond, plus a total). Open the Trophy Frogs menu at Researcher Ribery once to load your counts. After that, catches are counted from chat.\n- Counts are saved per account and SkyBlock profile.\n- Frogs you can't catch right now have their name struck through. Hover over one to see its requirements.\n- Hover to see the time until Trophy Frog pity. The tooltips also work while an inventory is open.\n- Only active on the Lotus Atoll.\n\n**Slayer**\n- Tracks the running slayer quest, with the boss read from the sidebar.\n- Pick an RNG drop for each slayer. Its RNG meter progress is shown above the action bar, and you get an alert when the meter is full. The drop list matches the current drops and the Aatrox buff.\n- Shows an estimate of the slayer kills left above the action bar.\n\n**HUD editor**\n- Open it with `/skysens hud` or the **Edit HUD Positions** button in General. Drag a HUD to move it, Ctrl + scroll to scale it, right click to reset it, and press Esc to save.\n\n**Notifications**\n- Notification levels, configurable per notification, next to each feature's options.\n- Optionally hold back notifications during combat, in dungeons and during slayer quests.\n\n**Party and co-op**\n- Party tracker that follows party events. `!warpto` now uses it.\n- Co-op members are tracked by profile id and through join/leave messages.\n- New `!uptime` command that shows a player's current session uptime.\n- Chat messages sent by commands are prefixed with an uncolored SkySens prefix.\n\n**Quality of life**\n- Option to hide the armor bar.\n- The SkySens action bar moves above Inventory HUD+ when they overlap.\n\n**Config screen**\n- Auto GUI scale for large screens, with sections listed in the sidebar and badges and Expand/Collapse all on section headers.\n- Reset an option or everything, with a confirmation step. Search results can be picked with the arrow keys and Enter.\n- Animated SkySens brand gradient.\n\n## Fixes\n- `!uptime` no longer resets on every server switch, and its time zone name accounts for daylight saving time.\n- Loot share skips drops worth 0 coins and treats soulbound drops as worthless.\n- Slayer book drops named only by their enchant are now priced.\n- The RNG meter progress no longer flickers.\n- Islands and zones are updated to the current SkyBlock.\n\n## Other\n- SkySens is now licensed under MIT.\n- Your settings carry over: options that moved are migrated automatically.\n\n## Changes since v1.0.16\n\n### New features\n- Generate descriptive changelogs for Modrinth and GitHub releases (#91)\n- Trophy Frogs: show the HUD tooltips with an inventory open (#88)\n- Trophy Frogs: time until pity on hover, only active on the Lotus Atoll (#87)\n- Strike through uncatchable Trophy Frogs and show requirements on hover (#86)\n- Add a HUD editor to move and scale SkySens HUDs (#85)\n- Party tracker with party events, used by !warpto (#83)\n- Move config migrations into ConfigMigration classes (#84)\n- Move notification levels next to their features' options (#82)\n- Track co-op members by profile id and from join/leave messages (#81)\n- Add a Trophy Frog HUD (#79)\n- QOL: move the action bar above Inventory HUD+ when they overlap (#80)\n- Add QOL option to hide the armor bar (#78)\n- Split alpha and beta Modrinth deployments (#72)\n- Draw RNG meter progress above the action bar to stop flickering (#71)\n- Show estimated slayer kills left in the action bar (#70)\n- Sync slayer RNG meter drops and Aatrox buff (#69)\n- Track a chosen slayer RNG drop per slayer with action bar and full alert (#68)\n- Add notification levels with a configurable level per notification (#67)\n- Animate the SkySens brand gradient in the config screen (#66)\n- Add a SlayerTracker for the running slayer quest (#65)\n- Add options to hold notifications in combat, dungeons and slayer quests (#64)\n- Rework the config screen navigation, scaling and reset flow (#62)\n\n..."
		},
